  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3703.04 Availability of Funds",
  "priorExpiration": "2017-03-14",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3703.04 Availability of Funds. If at any time the fund does not have money available to reimburse the application, the department shall:\n\n(a) Notify the applicant that the default bench warrant fund has insufficient funds for reimbursement;\n\n(b) Retain a chronological list of unreimbursed requests; and\n\n(c) As funds become available reimburse the applicant’s beginning with the oldest date on the list.\n\nSource. #6890, eff 1-1-99; ss by #8665, eff 6-19-06, EXPIRED: 6-19-14\n\nNew. #11175, INTERIM, eff 9-15-16, EXPIRES: 3-14-17; ss by #12120, eff 2-23-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3700.html"
